# OPTIONAL narrow sudo rule for the Memory and Swap Optimizer Agent.
# Install with:  sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/mso-agent   (replace "student" with your user)
#
# It permits exactly the privileged commands the agent's runner can build for
# the memory module -- nothing else.  It is NOT broad passwordless sudo:
#   * vm.swappiness only in 10..100 (matches security/policy.py)
#   * vm.drop_caches only 1, 2 or 3
# Without this file the agent still works; approved privileged actions simply
# fail with "sudo: a password is required" (sudo -n never prompts).
# Kernel-module and systemd actions are deliberately not included here.
student ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/sysctl -w vm.swappiness=[1-9][0-9], /usr/sbin/sysctl -w vm.swappiness=100, /usr/sbin/sysctl -w vm.drop_caches=1, /usr/sbin/sysctl -w vm.drop_caches=2, /usr/sbin/sysctl -w vm.drop_caches=3
